WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:10.290
Here's how to read the Hours this season card on your volunteer page. It looks a little different depending on how many volunteers and students are in your family.

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:15.749
One volunteer and one student: the big number is your hours this season.

00:00:15.949 --> 00:00:21.944
The box shows your student's total from everyone. It matches yours, because you're the only volunteer.

00:00:22.144 --> 00:00:27.150
Below that: hours not paid out yet, and anything still pending review.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.139
One volunteer and two students: the big number is still your hours.

00:00:32.339 --> 00:00:35.625
The bar splits them by the student each shift counted for.

00:00:35.825 --> 00:00:38.740
Each student gets a box with their total.

00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:43.409
Two volunteers and one student: the big number is your hours.

00:00:43.609 --> 00:00:50.650
The student's box adds up everyone who worked for them. Here, 31.5 hours from 2 volunteers.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:56.040
Pending review counts anyone in the family. Yours are on the line underneath.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:01:08.197
Two or more volunteers and two or more students: now the big number is the whole family's hours for your students. Here, 54 hours for 2 students, from 2 volunteers.

00:01:08.397 --> 00:01:12.060
Next to it are your hours: only the shifts you worked.

00:01:12.910 --> 00:01:15.428
The bar splits the family total by student.

00:01:15.628 --> 00:01:25.207
Each row is one student. Their total from everyone is on the right. Under it: your share, how many volunteers worked for them, and anything not paid out yet.

00:01:25.407 --> 00:01:36.530
The yellow box counts shifts waiting for the IU liaison to approve, for the whole family, with yours underneath. Once they're approved, the hours move into the totals.

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:43.390
Questions about your hours? Email the IU liaison from the bottom of any Hub page.
